WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.539
Onboarding is simple: show up, loop, ship.

00:00:02.539 --> 00:00:04.352
You are not collecting courses.

00:00:04.352 --> 00:00:07.253
This lesson is about from waitlist to student.

00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:09.067
How DigProg onboarding will work.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.605
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.605 --> 00:00:15.232
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:20.672
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.672 --> 00:00:24.661
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.661 --> 00:00:29.376
Stay practical: describe your first week plan before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:37.269
First week plan: finish Foundations lessons with quizzes, set your hour budget, write a kill criterion, and do one real outreach.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:40.155
Remember the objective: describe your first week plan.

00:00:40.155 --> 00:00:44.122
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:48.449
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:52.416
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:56.744
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:57.064 --> 00:01:03.835
Use the weekly loop every week: watch one lesson, take the quiz, do one action, then write a note.

00:01:03.835 --> 00:01:06.686
Remember the objective: describe your first week plan.

00:01:06.686 --> 00:01:10.607
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:14.883
